  {
   "id": "ai.action.breach",
   "kind": "ai",
   "owner": "13",
   "section": "13 4.7 Action catalog and behavior sets",
   "fields": {
    "weight": "7500",
    "considerations": "precondition: the agent's next path link is a breach link (§4.13)",
    "notes": "doc 07 §10.5; a channel action (§4.6) that lasts until the cell breaks: the agent faces the Errata-placed cell and strikes it on every tick `t0 + k × cycle_ticks` (`t0` the `Channel` start, `k ≥ 1`), each strike `damage_block(cell, B1, basic-attack shares, agent, 5000)` (doc 03 §13.2, the melee block factor; `B1` is the agent's ×1 basic-attack `B` of §2.2, whatever its basic attack's kind); placeables are `tooltier.t0`, so every strike counts; no token, no telegraph, no draw; when the cell breaks (cause `grid.cause.broken`) the §4.6 invalid-cell row ends the channel and the next think resumes the path"
   },
